            "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nextstrain/nextclade_data/tarball/2026-10-06--17-37-18Z",
            "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nextstrain/nextclade_data/zipball/2026-10-06--17-37-18Z",
            "body": "This release contains changes for datasets:\n\n- Bundibugyo ebolavirus (nextstrain/orthoebolavirus/bdbv)\n- DENV-1 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv1)\n- DENV-2 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv2)\n- DENV-3 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv3)\n- DENV-4 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv4)\n\n\n\n## Bundibugyo ebolavirus (nextstrain/orthoebolavirus/bdbv)\n\n - Update reference tree with more recent genomes\n - Include putative ADAR edit-detection. Cluster of 3 or more T->C mutations will now be highlighed.\n\n\n\n\n## DENV-1 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv1)\n\n- 2026 Annual update: added new lineages to the classification system as determined by the scientific committee.\n- Updated representative tree sequences to reduce assignment errors.\n- Outgroup sequences are now labeled `unassigned` instead of `Outgroup`.\n- Restored country coloring and the map using Pathoplexus country metadata where available.\n- Most reference-tree tips now use Pathoplexus accessions (`PP_...`) as their identifiers.\n- Corrected placement masks to match each serotype's GFF3 coding bounds and reference length.\n- New lineages: 1V_A.1, 1V_A.2, 1V_D.1.4, 1V_F.1, 1V_F.2\n\n\n\n\n## DENV-2 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv2)\n\n- 2026 Annual update: added new lineages to the classification system as determined by the scientific committee.\n- Updated representative tree sequences to reduce assignment errors.\n- Outgroup sequences are now labeled `unassigned` instead of `Outgroup`.\n- Restored country coloring and the map using Pathoplexus country metadata where available.\n- Most reference-tree tips now use Pathoplexus accessions (`PP_...`) as their identifiers.\n- Corrected placement masks to match each serotype's GFF3 coding bounds and reference length.\n- New lineages: 2III_C.3, 2III_D.1.2.1, 2III_D.1.2.2, 2III_D.1.2.3, 2II_D.4.1, 2II_D.4.2, 2II_F.1.1.10, 2II_F.1.1.2.1, 2II_F.1.1.2.2, 2II_F.1.1.2.3, 2II_F.1.1.9, 2V_F\n\n\n\n\n## DENV-3 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv3)\n\n- 2026 Annual update: added new lineages to the classification system as determined by the scientific committee.\n- Updated representative tree sequences to reduce assignment errors.\n- Outgroup sequences are now labeled `unassigned` instead of `Outgroup`.\n- Restored country coloring and the map using Pathoplexus country metadata where available.\n- Most reference-tree tips now use Pathoplexus accessions (`PP_...`) as their identifiers.\n- Corrected placement masks to match each serotype's GFF3 coding bounds and reference length.\n- New lineages: 3III_B.5, 3I_C.2.1, 3I_C.2.2, 3I_C.2.3\n\n\n\n\n## DENV-4 (community/v-gen-lab/dengue/denv4)\n\n- 2026 Annual update: added new lineages to the classification system as determined by the scientific committee.\n- Updated representative tree sequences to reduce assignment errors.\n- Outgroup sequences are now labeled `unassigned` instead of `Outgroup`.\n- Restored country coloring and the map using Pathoplexus country metadata where available.\n- Most reference-tree tips now use Pathoplexus accessions (`PP_...`) as their identifiers.\n- Corrected placement masks to match each serotype's GFF3 coding bounds and reference length.\n- New lineages: 4II_A.1.3, 4II_B.3\n\n\n\n",
